IMPORT prelude

-- Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886 (Singapore) -- what a buyer may demand of title (s 3(3), (4)), consent to assign a
-- lease (s 17), forfeiture of leases and relief (ss 18, 18A), a mortgagor's and mortgagee's rights on redemption, sale, insurance
-- and receivership (ss 21-29, selected), conveyances by deed in English (s 53), co-ownership (ss 66A, 73A), service of notices
-- (s 72), voluntary dispositions (s 73C) and the ceiling for offences under the conveyancing-money rules (s 73D(2)(h)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"), informal consolidation,
-- "version in force from 1/4/2022", as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CLPA1886.txt (retrieved 1 October 2026, "Current
-- version as at 01 Oct 2026"). The latest amendment annotated in the text is Act 25 of 2021 with effect from 1 April 2022.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0029 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to the provisions a home buyer, landlord, tenant, borrower, lender or co-owner most often meets. Not encoded:
-- general words and implied covenants for title (ss 6, 7), the remaining leasehold provisions (ss 10-16), transfer instead of
-- reconveyance and inspection of deeds (ss 19, 20), the court's sale powers (s 30), statutory mortgage forms (Part 5 and the
-- Schedule), court-made easements (Part 5A), devolution on death, married women, aliens, corporations and minors (Parts 6-8),
-- rentcharges, powers of attorney (Parts 9, 10), the rest of Part 11, powers, notice and adoption (Parts 12-14), life policies
-- (s 73), the content of the conveyancing-money rules and the adjudication scheme (ss 73D, 73E beyond the penalty ceiling) and
-- procedure (Part 16).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example rows. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886 -- leases, mortgages and co-owners`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` a b MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` a b MEANS
    IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `3 -- what a purchaser may demand of title`

-- s 3(3): recitals and statements of fact in deeds, instruments, Acts or statutory declarations "12 years old at the date of the
-- contract shall, unless and except so far as they are proved to be inaccurate, be taken to be sufficient evidence".
GIVEN `age of the recital in years` IS A NUMBER, `proved inaccurate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recital is sufficient evidence` IF
    `age of the recital in years` AT LEAST 12 AND (NOT `proved inaccurate`)

-- s 3(4): a purchaser "shall not be entitled to require a title to be deduced for a period of more than 15 years or for a period
-- extending further back than a grant or lease by the Crown or the State, whichever period is the shorter".
GIVEN `years since the State grant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the longest title period a purchaser may require in years` MEANS
    `the lesser of` 15 `years since the State grant`

§§ `17 -- consent to assign or under-let`

-- s 17(1): a covenant against assigning or under-letting without consent is "deemed to be subject to a proviso ... that no fine
-- or sum of money in the nature of a fine shall be payable" for the consent, "unless the lease contains an expressed provision to
-- the contrary"; but the landlord may require "a reasonable sum in respect of any legal or other expense incurred".
GIVEN `the lease expressly allows a fine` IS A BOOLEAN, `the sum is a reasonable legal or other expense` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the landlord may charge the sum for consent` IF
    `the lease expressly allows a fine` OR `the sum is a reasonable legal or other expense`

§§ `18 -- forfeiture for breach of covenant`

-- s 18(1): a right of re-entry or forfeiture "shall not be enforceable ... unless the lessor serves on the lessee a notice
-- specifying the particular breach", requiring it to be remedied "if the breach is capable of remedy" and requiring compensation,
-- "and the lessee fails, within a reasonable time thereafter, to remedy the breach, if it is capable of remedy, and to make
-- reasonable compensation". (8): the section does not extend to a covenant against assigning, under-letting or parting with
-- possession, nor to forfeiture on bankruptcy or on the taking in execution of the lessee's interest. (9): it does not affect the
-- law on non-payment of rent (for which see s 18A). (10): it has effect "notwithstanding any stipulation to the contrary".
DECLARE Breach IS ONE OF
    `failure to repair`
    `use contrary to the user covenant`
    `assigning without consent`
    `under-letting without consent`
    `bankruptcy of the lessee`
    `execution against the lessee's interest`
    `non-payment of rent`

GIVEN `the breach` IS A Breach
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 18 notice is required before forfeiture` IF
    CONSIDER `the breach`
    WHEN `failure to repair` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `use contrary to the user covenant` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Reading of s 18(1): enforceable only if the notice was served AND the lessee failed to do what was required of him within a
-- reasonable time (remedy, where remediable, and compensation). The "reasonable time" is not modelled; the flags are its outcome.
GIVEN `notice served` IS A BOOLEAN, `capable of remedy` IS A BOOLEAN, `remedied in reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `compensated in reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `forfeiture for the breach is enforceable` IF
    `notice served` AND NOT (((NOT `capable of remedy`) OR `remedied in reasonable time`) AND `compensated in reasonable time`)

§§ `18A -- relief against forfeiture for non-payment of rent`

-- s 18A(2): if, within the time for acknowledging service of the writ, "the lessee pays into court all the rent in arrear and the
-- costs of the action, the action shall cease, and the lessee shall hold the land according to the lease without any new lease".
-- (6): (2) does not apply where the lessor also claims forfeiture on another ground or makes another claim in the same action.
GIVEN `paid all arrears and costs into court in time` IS A BOOLEAN, `the action also claims on another ground` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rent action ceases` IF
    `paid all arrears and costs into court in time` AND (NOT `the action also claims on another ground`)

-- s 18A(3): the court orders possession "at the expiration of such period, but not being less than 4 weeks from the date of the
-- order". Encoded in days: 4 weeks = 28 days.
GIVEN `days from the order to possession` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the possession period is permitted` IF
    `days from the order to possession` AT LEAST 28

§§ `21, 22 -- redemption`

-- s 21(1): a mortgagor may redeem one mortgage "without paying any money due under any separate mortgage" on other property;
-- (2) "only if and so far as a contrary intention is not expressed in the mortgage deeds or one of them".
GIVEN `a mortgage deed reserves consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mortgagor may redeem one mortgage alone` IF
    NOT `a mortgage deed reserves consolidation`

-- s 22(1): where the mortgage money "is not paid on the stated day", the mortgagee is entitled, absent a contrary stipulation, "to
-- 3 months' notice in writing previous to payment or to 3 months' interest in lieu of that notice".
GIVEN `paid on the stated day` IS A BOOLEAN, `the deed stipulates otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mortgagee may insist on 3 months' notice or interest` IF
    (NOT `paid on the stated day`) AND (NOT `the deed stipulates otherwise`)

-- Simple interest at the mortgage rate for a quarter of a year (an inference: the Act does not say how the 3 months' interest is
-- computed).
GIVEN `mortgage money` IS A NUMBER, `annual interest rate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`3 months' interest in lieu of notice` MEANS
    `mortgage money` TIMES `annual interest rate` DIVIDED BY 4

§§ `23 -- leasing powers of a mortgagor or mortgagee in possession`

-- s 23(1): a mortgagor in possession may make "an agricultural or occupation lease ... for any term not exceeding 3 years". (2) a
-- mortgagee in possession may make (a) an agricultural or occupation lease "not exceeding 21 years"; (b) a building lease "not
-- exceeding 99 years". (4) every such lease must take effect in possession "not later than 12 months after its date"; (6) it must
-- contain a condition of re-entry on rent not being paid within a time "not exceeding 30 days". (11) the section yields to a
-- contrary intention in the mortgage deed (not modelled).
DECLARE `Leasing party` IS ONE OF `a mortgagor in possession`, `a mortgagee in possession`
DECLARE `Lease kind` IS ONE OF `an agricultural or occupation lease`, `a building lease`

GIVEN `the party` IS A `Leasing party`, `the kind` IS A `Lease kind`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the longest statutory term in years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the party`
    WHEN `a mortgagor in possession` THEN
        CONSIDER `the kind`
        WHEN `an agricultural or occupation lease` THEN 3
        WHEN `a building lease` THEN 0
    WHEN `a mortgagee in possession` THEN
        CONSIDER `the kind`
        WHEN `an agricultural or occupation lease` THEN 21
        WHEN `a building lease` THEN 99

GIVEN `the party` IS A `Leasing party`, `the kind` IS A `Lease kind`, `term in years` IS A NUMBER,
      `months until possession` IS A NUMBER, `days allowed before re-entry` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lease is within the statutory leasing power` IF
        `term in years` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `term in years` AT MOST `the longest statutory term in years` `the party` `the kind`
    AND `months until possession` AT MOST 12
    AND `days allowed before re-entry` AT MOST 30

§§ `24, 25, 29(1) -- when the mortgagee may sell or appoint a receiver`

-- s 24(1): a mortgagee, "where the mortgage is made by deed", has "(a) a power, when the mortgage money has become due, to sell";
-- (3) subject to a contrary intention in the deed. s 25: the power "shall not" be exercised unless (a) notice requiring payment
-- has been served and "default has been made ... for 3 months after the service"; (b) "some interest under the mortgage is in
-- arrears and unpaid for one month after becoming due"; or (c) a breach of some other provision of the deed or the Act.
-- s 29(1): a receiver may not be appointed "until he has become entitled to exercise the power of sale".
GIVEN `made by deed` IS A BOOLEAN, `mortgage money due` IS A BOOLEAN, `the deed excludes the power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mortgagee has the statutory power of sale` IF
    `made by deed` AND `mortgage money due` AND (NOT `the deed excludes the power`)

GIVEN `payment demanded by notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `months of default after the notice` IS A NUMBER,
      `months interest has been unpaid` IS A NUMBER, `other breach of the deed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the power of sale is exercisable` IF
        (`payment demanded by notice` AND `months of default after the notice` AT LEAST 3)
    OR  `months interest has been unpaid` AT LEAST 1
    OR  `other breach of the deed`

GIVEN `payment demanded by notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `months of default after the notice` IS A NUMBER,
      `months interest has been unpaid` IS A NUMBER, `other breach of the deed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mortgagee may appoint a receiver` IF
    `the power of sale is exercisable` `payment demanded by notice` `months of default after the notice` `months interest has been unpaid` `other breach of the deed`

§§ `26 -- the sale and its proceeds`

-- s 26(2): the purchaser's title "shall not be impeachable on the ground that no case had arisen to authorise the sale, or that due
-- notice was not given"; "any person damnified ... shall have his remedy in damages against the person exercising the power".
GIVEN `the sale was irregular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purchaser's title can be impeached` IF
    FALSE

GIVEN `the sale was irregular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner may claim damages from the selling mortgagee` IF
    `the sale was irregular`

-- s 26(3): after discharge of prior incumbrances, the proceeds are held on trust "first, in payment of all costs, charges and
-- expenses" of the sale; "secondly, in discharge of the mortgage money, interest and costs"; "the residue ... shall be paid to the
-- person entitled to the mortgaged property". A shortfall is not dealt with by this section (the residue floors at nil here).
GIVEN `sale price` IS A NUMBER, `prior incumbrances` IS A NUMBER, `costs of sale` IS A NUMBER, `owed under the mortgage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the residue for the owner` MEANS
    `the greater of` 0 (`sale price` MINUS `prior incumbrances` MINUS `costs of sale` MINUS `owed under the mortgage`)

§§ `28 -- fire insurance by the mortgagee`

-- s 28(1): the insurance "shall not exceed the amount specified for that purpose in the mortgage deed, or, if no such amount is
-- therein specified, then shall not exceed two-third parts of the amount that would be required, in case of total destruction, to
-- restore the property insured". Here 0 stands for "no amount specified".
GIVEN `amount specified in the deed` IS A NUMBER, `cost to restore after total destruction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the mortgagee may insure for` MEANS
    IF `amount specified in the deed` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `amount specified in the deed`
    ELSE `cost to restore after total destruction` TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 3

-- s 28(2): no insurance under the Act (a) where the deed declares none is required; (b) where the mortgagor keeps up insurance in
-- accordance with the deed; (c) where the deed is silent and the mortgagor keeps up insurance, "with the knowledge of the
-- mortgagee", to the amount the mortgagee could insure for.
GIVEN `the deed says no insurance is required` IS A BOOLEAN, `the mortgagor insures as the deed requires` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the deed is silent on insurance` IS A BOOLEAN, `the mortgagor insures to the full amount to the mortgagee's knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mortgagee may insure under the Act` IF
        (NOT `the deed says no insurance is required`)
    AND (NOT `the mortgagor insures as the deed requires`)
    AND NOT (`the deed is silent on insurance` AND `the mortgagor insures to the full amount to the mortgagee's knowledge`)

§§ `29(6) -- the receiver's commission`

-- s 29(6): the receiver may retain "a commission at such rate, not exceeding 5% on the gross amount of all money received, as is
-- specified in his appointment, and if no rate is so specified, then at the rate of 5%". Here 0 stands for "no rate specified"; a
-- specified rate above 5% is capped at 5% (an inference from "not exceeding").
GIVEN `rate specified in the appointment` IS A NUMBER, `gross money received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the receiver's commission` MEANS
    IF `rate specified in the appointment` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `gross money received` TIMES `the lesser of` `rate specified in the appointment` 0.05
    ELSE `gross money received` TIMES 0.05

§§ `53 -- conveyance by deed in English`

-- s 53(1): "A conveyance of any estate or interest in land other than a lease for a period not exceeding 7 years at a rack rent
-- shall be void at law unless it is by deed in the English language." (2): only conveyances executed on or after 1 March 1994.
GIVEN `a lease of at most 7 years at a rack rent` IS A BOOLEAN, `executed on or after 1 March 1994` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `by deed` IS A BOOLEAN, `in English` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conveyance is void at law` IF
        (NOT `a lease of at most 7 years at a rack rent`)
    AND `executed on or after 1 March 1994`
    AND NOT (`by deed` AND `in English`)

§§ `66A, 73A -- joint tenants and tenants in common`

-- s 66A(1): "Tenants in common entitled in equal shares" may by deed of declaration hold as joint tenants.
GIVEN `the shares are equal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `tenants in common may declare a joint tenancy` IF
    `the shares are equal`

-- s 66A(3), (4): a joint tenant may sever by deed of declaration served on the other joint tenants; the declarant then holds as
-- tenant in common "a share that is equal in proportion to each of the remaining joint tenants". (6): a copy sent by registered
-- post is deemed served "2 days after the day it is sent ... notwithstanding it is returned undelivered".
GIVEN `number of joint tenants` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the severing joint tenant's share` MEANS
    1 DIVIDED BY `number of joint tenants`

GIVEN `day posted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day the severance deed is deemed served` MEANS
    `day posted` PLUS 2

-- s 73A: a co-owner "shall be liable to account to his co-owner for receiving more than his share or proportion of any rents or
-- profits arising from the property". The amount owed is taken here as the excess over his share (an inference).
GIVEN `rents received by him` IS A NUMBER, `total rents` IS A NUMBER, `his share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the excess a co-owner must account for` MEANS
    `the greater of` 0 (`rents received by him` MINUS `total rents` TIMES `his share`)

§§ `72 -- service of notices`

-- s 72(4): a notice is also sufficiently served if sent "in a registered letter" to the person by name at the last known abode or
-- business "and if that letter is not returned through the post office undelivered". (5): not notices in court proceedings.
-- Contrast s 66A(6), where a returned severance deed is still deemed served.
GIVEN `sent by registered post to the right address` IS A BOOLEAN, `returned undelivered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a notice in court proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice is served by post under s 72` IF
    `sent by registered post to the right address` AND (NOT `returned undelivered`) AND (NOT `a notice in court proceedings`)

§§ `73C -- voluntary dispositions`

-- s 73C(1): "Every voluntary disposition of immovable property made with intent to defraud a subsequent purchaser is voidable at the
-- instance of that purchaser." (2): no intent to defraud is deemed "by reason only that a subsequent disposition for valuable
-- consideration was made". The second flag records that the only evidence of intent is the later sale.
GIVEN `the disposition was voluntary` IS A BOOLEAN, `intent to defraud is proved` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the only evidence is the later sale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the later purchaser may avoid the gift` IF
    `the disposition was voluntary` AND `intent to defraud is proved` AND (NOT `the only evidence is the later sale`)

§§ `73D(2)(h) -- offences under the conveyancing-money rules`

-- s 73D(2)(h): the rules may make a contravention "an offence punishable with a fine not exceeding $50,000 or with imprisonment for a
-- term not exceeding 3 years or with both". (5): the Public Prosecutor may compound.
`the maximum fine under the conveyancing rules` MEANS 50000

`the maximum imprisonment in years under the conveyancing rules` MEANS 3
